  "cut": false,
  "source": "# The corridor of three doors\n\nKydux's own art, made for the game and under the GNU GPL, version 3 or\nlater, like the rest of it.\n\n- Painted by Gemini 3 Pro Image (`gemini-3-pro-image`) from\n  `tools/art/prompts/scene-four-doors.md`, then edited by it without its\n  grid (`game-three-doors-nogrid.md`).\n- What it left black along the top and in the bottom corners painted by Gemini\n  from `game-three-doors-voids.md`, joined by `tools/art/repaint.py`, and\n  what still was black tiled from the picture's own stones (`tiled`).\n- Its three walls moved along their rows by `tools/art/repaint.py spaced`, so\n  that the doors lie exactly four cells apart.\n- Each door's doorway opened by `tools/art/repaint.py doorways`, and each leaf\n  swung open painted by Gemini (`game-three-doors-swung-1.md`, `-2`, `-3`) in\n  a box, joined by `tools/art/repaint.py`.\n",
  "voids": {
    "about": "What the model left black along the top edge and in the bottom corners painted as the castle's inside (D136), the top arch's dark kept: by Gemini 3 Pro Image from tools/art/prompts/game-three-doors-voids.md on the canvas this makes, and joined by tools/art/repaint.py, the painting kept pixel for pixel elsewhere.",
